<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-chP-vocab" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title> Vocabulary </title>
    
    <definition xml:id="def-pop">
      <title>Population</title> <idx>Population</idx>
      <p> A population is the entire group of individuals or items that we are interested in studying. 
        For example, if we are interested in studying the average height of all college students in the 
        United States, then the population would be all college students in the United States. 
      </p>
   </definition>
   

   <definition xml:id="def-sample">
      <title>Sample</title>
      <p> A sample is a subset of the population that we actually study. For example, if we take a 
       random sample of 100 college students from the population of all college students in the 
       United States, then that sample would be used to estimate the average height of all college 
       students in the United States. 
      </p>
    </definition>

</section>